.TH COMPUST.TOML 5 2026-11-14 Compust "File Formats"
.nh
.SH NAME
compust.toml \- configuration of the compust compositor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/compust/compust.toml
.br
.I $XDG_CONFIG_DIRS/compust/compust.toml
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR compust (1)
reads its settings from a TOML file: the one that
.B \-\-config
names, or else the first
.I compust/compust.toml
in
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME
(by default
.IR ~/.config ),
then in each directory of
.B $XDG_CONFIG_DIRS
(by default
.IR /etc/xdg ).
Without a file, the defaults below apply.
.PP
The file holds the global settings, then any number of
.B [[rules]]
tables, which set some of them for chosen windows.
Every setting is optional.
An unknown setting, a value of the wrong type, or a value out of its range
is an error;
.B compust \-\-check\-config
reports it without connecting to the X server.
.PP
Saving the file, or sending
.BR SIGUSR1 ,
reloads it.
.BR opacity ,
.BR max_fps ,
.BR unredirect_fullscreen ,
the shadow settings, and the opacity, blur, and shadow that rules give apply
from the next frame, to windows already open too.
A new
.BR fade_ms ,
global or in a rule, applies to every opening and closing that starts
afterward; fades in progress finish with their previous duration.
A change to
.BR blur_radius ,
.BR vsync ,
or
.B backend
replaces the renderer once the frame being presented is done.
An invalid file is logged and leaves the running settings unchanged.
.SH GLOBAL SETTINGS
.TP
.BR opacity " (integer, 0 to 100, default 100)"
The opacity of every window, in percent.
It multiplies the opacity that an application sets in
.BR _NET_WM_WINDOW_OPACITY .
.TP
.BR fade_ms " (integer, 0 to 65535, default 180)"
How long a window takes to fade in when it opens and out when it closes, in
milliseconds.
Zero turns fades off.
.TP
.BR blur_radius " (integer, 0 to 16, default 4)"
The approximate radius, in pixels, of the blur behind translucent windows,
rounded to 2, 4, 8, or 16.
The blur shows through each pixel as strongly as the window covers it, so a
transparent margin stays sharp, and it fades with its window.
Zero turns blur off.
Without a bilinear filter in the server, Compust logs a warning and runs
without blur.
.TP
.BR shadow_radius " (integer, 0 to 64, default 0)"
How far a shadow spreads beyond its window, in pixels.
Zero draws no shadows.
A shadow is the window's rectangle, moved by the offset and blurred over
this radius; it lies around its window, never beneath it, and fades with it.
.TP
.BR shadow_offset_x ", " shadow_offset_y " (integers, \-64 to 64, default 0)"
Where a shadow lies from its window, in pixels: to the right and down, or to
the left and up when negative.
.TP
.BR shadow_opacity " (integer, 0 to 100, default 50)"
How dark a shadow is where it is darkest, in percent, multiplied by its
window's opacity.
.TP
.BR corner_radius " (integer, 0 to 64, default 0)"
The radius of rounded window corners, in pixels.
Zero keeps corners square.
A window's shadow and the blur behind it follow its corners, and a radius
never exceeds half of the window's shorter side.
.TP
.BR max_fps " (integer, 1 to 1000, default 120)"
The most frames drawn in a second.
It does not make an idle desktop repaint.
.TP
.BR vsync " (boolean, default true)"
Present finished frames through the Present extension, in step with the
display, where the server supports it.
.B false
copies them directly, without synchronization to vertical blanking.
.TP
.BR backend " (string, default \(dqxrender\(dq)"
.B \(dqxrender\(dq
draws through the X server.
.B \(dqgl\(dq
draws with OpenGL ES on the server's GPU, through DRI3 1.2 and EGL, and falls
back to XRender with a warning where it cannot.
.TP
.BR unredirect_fullscreen " (boolean, default false)"
.B true
stops compositing while the topmost window is opaque, has no shape or
rounded corners, and covers the whole screen, as a fullscreen game or video
does; windows then draw to the screen directly.
Compositing resumes as soon as that stops being true.
One overlay covers every monitor, so a window that fills one of several
monitors stays composited.
.SH SHADOWS AND CORNERS BY WINDOW TYPE
Windows of the types
.BR normal ,
.BR dialog ,
.BR utility ,
.BR splash ,
and
.B toolbar
cast shadows and have their corners rounded.
Other types, a window that names no type and that the window manager does
not manage, and a window that declares margins for its own decorations in
.B _GTK_FRAME_EXTENTS
get neither.
A window with a shape of its own gets neither, and a window that the window
manager shows fullscreen keeps square corners.
A rule's
.B shadow
and
.B corner_radius
decide for the windows it chooses.
.SH RULES
Each
.B [[rules]]
table chooses windows by one or more of these fields; a window must match
all of those that the rule gives:
.TP
.BR wm_class " (string)"
The resource class, the second string of
.BR WM_CLASS .
.TP
.BR window_type " (string)"
The EWMH type:
.BR desktop ,
.BR dock ,
.BR toolbar ,
.BR menu ,
.BR utility ,
.BR splash ,
.BR dialog ,
.BR dropdown_menu ,
.BR popup_menu ,
.BR tooltip ,
.BR notification ,
.BR combo ,
.BR dnd ,
or
.BR normal .
A window that names no type that Compust knows is
.B dialog
when it is transient for another window and managed by the window manager,
and
.B normal
otherwise.
.TP
.BR name " (string)"
The title,
.B _NET_WM_NAME
or else
.BR WM_NAME .
.TP
.BR focused " (boolean)"
.B true
chooses the window that the window manager names in the root's
.BR _NET_ACTIVE_WINDOW ;
.B false
chooses every other window, menus and docks included.
Under a window manager that does not set that property, every window counts
as focused.
.PP
It sets one or more of these:
.TP
.BR opacity " (integer, 0 to 100)"
Used instead of the global
.BR opacity .
.TP
.BR blur " (boolean)"
.B false
keeps what lies behind the window sharp;
.B true
blurs it as by default, while
.B blur_radius
is above zero.
.TP
.BR fade_ms " (integer, 0 to 65535)"
Used instead of the global
.BR fade_ms .
.TP
.BR shadow " (boolean)"
.B false
gives the window no shadow;
.B true
gives it one whatever its type or margins, while
.B shadow_radius
is above zero.
.TP
.BR corner_radius " (integer, 0 to 64)"
Used instead of the global
.B corner_radius
whatever the window's type or margins;
.B 0
keeps it square.
.PP
Text matches exactly, including case.
Each setting comes from the first matching rule that sets it, so specific
rules go before broad ones.
Compust reads these properties from the application's window inside the
window manager's frame, again whenever they change, and a closing window
keeps the rules it had while it fades out.
.BR xprop (1)
shows a window's
.BR WM_CLASS ,
.BR _NET_WM_WINDOW_TYPE ,
and
.BR _NET_WM_NAME .
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.EX
fade_ms = 160
blur_radius = 8
shadow_radius = 10
shadow_offset_x = 4
shadow_offset_y = 4
corner_radius = 8
backend = "gl"

# Terminals at 90% opacity, with square corners.
[[rules]]
wm_class = "Alacritty"
opacity = 90
corner_radius = 0

# Tooltips without blur behind them, and without fades.
[[rules]]
window_type = "tooltip"
blur = false
fade_ms = 0

# Normal windows other than the active one at 85% opacity.
[[rules]]
window_type = "normal"
focused = false
opacity = 85
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR compust (1),
.BR xprop (1)
